    "rationale": "RENAMED + REWRITTEN 2026-08-26 (was `dym-first-pick-still-uses-the-for-hint-fallback`). The original pinned the issue-#30 boundary in the other direction - \"the for_hint fallback must still fire for the FIRST pick of a numbered turn, so A-1 replaces B-OLD IN PLACE: one entity out, no dym_replace_unmatched\" - and said in as many words that it would go red if the fix were ever widened to the whole numbered path. It was, on 2026-08-24, and this fixture went red on exactly that sentence. applyDymPick now gates BOTH the dym_slot tier and the for_hint tier on `_useSlot !== false`, and the numbered/accumulating multi-pick path passes `_useSlot = false`, because a hint is a TYPE and not an identity: with an unrelated product pinned beside the missed token, that tier REPLACED the unrelated product and silently dropped one of the two things the customer asked for. So a pick that cannot be tied to its source token by for_raw or for_canonical now APPENDS. That is what is pinned here: two entities out (A-1 prepended, B-OLD retained) and `dym_replace_unmatched: true`.",
